1.5.0: the darkroom release

Three upgrades from film-characterization practice:

Tetrahedral LUT interpolation replaces trilinear - the industry
standard, better neutral-axis and hue behavior between lattice points
at the same cost.

Age v2: storage degradation becomes per-process differential dye fade.
fade[] rates decay each channel's density toward base white, so the
drift emerges from the chemistry instead of being painted on: slide
goes red-magenta (cyan dies first), scanned C-41 cools, instant prints
amber, black-and-white only fogs with a faint warm stain. The film's
process selects the profile; with --no-film, cameras that imply
exactly one process (35mm-slide, polaroid-600, ...) supply it via the
new pj_preset_primary_process().

Print axis: --print chains a second .cube after the film transform -
the cinema negative->print model. Its own catalog category and web
selector, never mixed into films; engine, both CLIs, wasm and the page
all carry it, with tests at every layer (chained-transform effect in
core and engine, selector separation and in-page render on the page).

README gains the architecture section: F -> P -> develop -> A -> S,
with the measured-versus-inspired sourcing vocabulary in
PRESET_SOURCES.
